name    mod-kill-collector: the token shop sells every class buff at +50% for one hour, 10 Hunter's Tokens each
# Server-side test bot run (mod-fl-testbots), T1. Needs KillCollector.Enable = 1, fl-lua-scripts' TokenShop/ (the
# buff rows, branch claude/token-shop-buffs-433902b4) loaded by ALE (`.reload ale` after a deploy) and this folder in
# TestBots.ScenarioDirs. The bots buy through the chat command `.tokenshop buy <key>`, which runs the very function
# the window's Buy button reaches. The exact amounts are read back with the GM's `.list auras id <spell>`, which
# prints "id: <spell> eff: <n> amount: <amount>" for every effect of the aura on the selected unit.
#
# The shop casts the ORIGINAL spell (top rank) on the buyer, every amount x1.5 rounded half up, the aura set to 1 hour:
#   Power Word: Fortitude 48161   stamina 165 -> 248
#   Mark of the Wild      48469   armor 750 -> 1125, all stats 37 -> 56, all resistances 54 -> 81
#   Power Module (Tinker) 707688  attack power 232 -> 348, ranged attack power 232 -> 348 (a CoA spell bought by a mage)
#   Blessing of Sanctuary 20911 + 67480 (its script's aura: +10% stamina, strength -> +15%)
#   Blessing of Kings     20217   (the core keeps one of Kings/Sanctuary per caster: Kings replaces Sanctuary)
#   Battle Shout          47436   attack power 550 at level 80 (548 + 2 for the level) -> 825, ranged 825; an area spell:
#                                 the party members it reaches get nothing to keep (the shop takes the aura back)
#   Sanguinary Offering   707340  (Bloodmage) stamina 79 -> 119
#
# Parts 1-7 are the shop's own behaviour. Part 8 (a normal cast of the same spell by another player landing on a
# shop buff) is the core's stack rule, written down from the core source and to be confirmed by this run:
#   - a spell in no stack group (Power Word: Fortitude): the newer aura of another caster replaces the older one, so a
#     normal cast on a shop buff takes it down to the normal amount and duration;
#   - a spell in an EXCLUSIVE_HIGHEST group (Sanguinary Offering, group 2100004): the higher amount stays, the weaker
#     new aura is dropped, so the shop buff survives a normal cast.
#
# Repeatable: the start destroys the tokens and removes every aura named above; the cleanup does the same.
timeout 240s

bot a mage
bot b priest
bot c warrior
bot d bloodmage
place 0 -10.3 -1111.9 36.1
require a alive
require b alive
require c alive
require d alive
do a level 80
do c level 80
do gm target a
as gm .unaura 48161
as gm .unaura 48469
as gm .unaura 707688
as gm .unaura 20911
as gm .unaura 67480
as gm .unaura 20217
as gm .unaura 707340
do gm target c
as gm .unaura 47436
do a destroy 920200
do c destroy 920200
expect a item 920200 == 0
expect a noaura 48161

log 1 - the list: every buff group, stock and CoA, 10 tokens
as a .tokenshop list buffs
expect output has "-- Buffs: Priest"
expect output has "buff_power_word_fortitude: Power Word: Fortitude, 10 tokens"
expect output has "-- Buffs: Tinker"
expect output has "buff_power_module"
expect output has "-- Buffs: Runemaster"
expect output has "buff_battle_shout"
expect output has "buff_horn_of_winter"

log 2 - too few tokens: refused, no aura, nothing taken
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_word_fortitude
expect output has "Needs 10 Hunter's Tokens"
expect a noaura 48161
as a .tokenshop buy buff_no_such_thing
expect output has "no such shop entry"
as gm .additem Tbmaga 920200 100
expect a item 920200 == 100

log 3 - Power Word: Fortitude: stamina 165 x1.5 = 248 for an hour, 10 tokens
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_word_fortitude
expect output has "You buy Power Word: Fortitude (+50%, 1 hour) for 10 Hunter's Tokens"
expect output lacks "replaced"
expect a aura 48161
expect a auramaxduration 48161 >= 3500000
expect a auraduration 48161 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 90
do gm target a
as gm .list auras id 48161
expect output has "id: 48161 eff: 0 amount: 248"

log 4 - buying it again renews it (allowed), the answer says it replaced the one on the bot
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_word_fortitude
expect output has "replaced the same buff"
expect a aura 48161
expect a auraduration 48161 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 80
as gm .list auras id 48161
expect output has "id: 48161 eff: 0 amount: 248"

log 5 - Mark of the Wild (three effects) and a CoA buff bought by a mage (Tinker's Power Module)
as a .tokenshop buy buff_mark_of_the_wild
expect output has "You buy Mark of the Wild"
expect a auramaxduration 48469 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 70
as gm .list auras id 48469
expect output has "id: 48469 eff: 0 amount: 1125"
expect output has "id: 48469 eff: 1 amount: 56"
expect output has "id: 48469 eff: 2 amount: 81"
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_module
expect output has "You buy Power Module"
expect a aura 707688
expect a auramaxduration 707688 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 60
as gm .list auras id 707688
expect output has "id: 707688 eff: 0 amount: 348"
expect output has "id: 707688 eff: 1 amount: 348"

log 6 - Blessing of Sanctuary (the shop boosts the aura its script casts) and Kings (one of the two per caster)
as a .tokenshop buy buff_blessing_of_sanctuary
expect output has "You buy Blessing of Sanctuary"
expect a aura 20911
expect a auramaxduration 20911 >= 3500000
expect a aura 67480
expect a auramaxduration 67480 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 50
as gm .list auras id 67480
expect output has "id: 67480 eff: 0 amount: 15"
expect output has "id: 67480 eff: 1 amount: 15"
as a .tokenshop buy buff_blessing_of_kings
expect output has "You buy Blessing of Kings"
expect a aura 20217
expect a auramaxduration 20217 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 40
as gm .list auras id 20217
expect output has "id: 20217 eff: 0 amount: 15"
# the core's per-caster rule for Kings and Sanctuary (spell_group 1010): Kings took Sanctuary down
expect a noaura 20911

log 7 - Battle Shout, an area spell: the warrior keeps it for an hour at 825, the party gets nothing to keep
as gm .additem Tbwarc 920200 10
expect c item 920200 == 10
as c .tokenshop buy buff_battle_shout
expect output has "You buy Battle Shout"
expect c aura 47436
expect c auramaxduration 47436 >= 3500000
expect c item 920200 == 0
do gm target c
as gm .list auras id 47436
expect output has "id: 47436 eff: 0 amount: 825"
expect output has "id: 47436 eff: 1 amount: 825"
expect a noaura 47436
expect b noaura 47436
expect gm noaura 47436

log 8 - a normal cast by another player on a shop buff (the core's stack rule, see the header)
# Sanguinary Offering (Bloodmage, exclusive-highest group): the mage buys it, the bloodmage casts the normal one
as a .tokenshop buy buff_sanguinary_offering
expect output has "You buy Sanguinary Offering"
expect a item 920200 == 30
do gm target a
as gm .list auras id 707340
expect output has "id: 707340 eff: 0 amount: 119"
do d cast 707340 on a triggered
wait 1s
as gm .list auras id 707340
expect output has "id: 707340 eff: 0 amount: 119"
expect a auramaxduration 707340 >= 3500000
# Power Word: Fortitude (no stack group): the priest's normal cast replaces the shop buff
as gm .list auras id 48161
expect output has "id: 48161 eff: 0 amount: 248"
do b cast 48161 on a triggered
wait 1s
as gm .list auras id 48161
expect output has "id: 48161 eff: 0 amount: 165"
expect a auramaxduration 48161 <= 1800000

cleanup
do gm target a
as gm .unaura 48161
as gm .unaura 48469
as gm .unaura 707688
as gm .unaura 20911
as gm .unaura 67480
as gm .unaura 20217
as gm .unaura 707340
do gm target c
as gm .unaura 47436
do a destroy 920200
do c destroy 920200
log token shop buffs done
